{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"submission\": \"submission.json\",\n  \"summary\": \"Submitted a research product that closes two explanation-shaped frontier items with sourced reasoning.\\n\\nContext from the index: all three findings are confirmed_in_scope, map v6 is the accepted basis, pending_work is empty, and capacity still holds 1 audit unit, 3 semantic reviews and 5 experiments.\\n\\nProduct contents (draft-relative submission.json with the updated map.json):\\n\\nMap clarifications, both with source citations. b-prevote replaces the suspicion that treating an unsupported pre-vote as granting could let a partitioned candidate believe it would win: the round changes no state or term and winning it only starts a real election decided by real votes under the same membership, prior-vote and log-up-to-dateness checks; the residual is the mixed-version case, where an inflated tally can cause avoidable election churn rather than a wrong leader. b-leadership-transfer replaces its open TimeoutNow-validation question with the sourced consequence that a request whose term and sender are not consulted can only start a candidacy, since the campaign still needs a majority of the latest configuration's real votes; the residual is the repeated-election-round liveness case.\\n\\nThe accompanying feedback (ref_ids b-prevote, b-leadership-transfer) records both answered propositions, keeps the liveness residuals explicit, and refreshes the remaining frontier: restart survival of an unsupported committed configuration, the election-restriction chain and the heartbeat term-regression pair, the processHeartbeat shutdown non-response, the external consumers of the configuration index, and the majority-intersection residual. One audit unit is deliberately left unspent for a further executable question rather than consumed on these liveness residuals.\\n\\nPreflight `validate` returned valid=true with no diagnostics. Acceptance and version assignment remain with the controller.\"\n}"}}
